  "traps": [
    "two workspaces share the root: package.json declares a Bun workspace (frontend, packages/*) and pyproject.toml is a virtual uv workspace root (members = [\"backend\"]) with no [project] table, so the root gives one npm unit and one unnamed Python unit",
    "the uv root holds the dependency groups dev (prek, typer, zizmor) and github-actions (smokeshow) used by scripts/; with no project name they cannot be attributed to a named unit, so dependencies are complete only for app, emails and the root npm package",
    "the Python project is named app and its package is backend/app: the source root is backend, not the repository root",
    "the Bun workspace member packages/react-email is named emails, while the Python unit app depends on an unrelated PyPI package also named emails",
    "bun.lock names the workspace root fastapi-cloud while package.json says fastapi-full-stack-template: the lockfile root name is stale and package.json wins",
    "the root package.json has no packageManager, engines or Bun version: Bun is declared only by bun.lock, the Dockerfiles (oven/bun:1, bun install) and the setup-bun steps (1.3.12)",
    "the pre-commit hook runs npm run lint, but nothing else uses npm: the package manager is Bun",
    "Python 3.14 is asked four ways: requires-python >=3.14,<4.0, .python-version 3.14, Ruff target-version py314 and FROM python:3.14; every workflow reads .python-version through python-version-file instead of writing a version",
    "setup-uv asks for version latest-known in every workflow; the only fixed uv version is the image ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:0.9.26 copied in backend/Dockerfile",
    "frontend/Dockerfile.playwright starts from mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.64.1-noble, which carries Node, and installs Bun from a script with no version: neither is listed as a toolchain",
    "frontend/src/client/ is generated by @hey-api/openapi-ts from frontend/openapi.json, which is git-ignored and produced by scripts/generate-client.sh importing app.main: the client is checked in, its input is not",
    "the Vite build writes to ../backend/app/frontend (git-ignored), which FastAPI serves with app.frontend(\"/\") and backend/Dockerfile copies from a Bun build stage: the back-end image builds the front end",
    "backend/app/email-templates/*.html are checked-in exports of packages/react-email (email export --outDir ../../backend/app/email-templates), rendered by the back end with Jinja2: the HTML carries {{ }} placeholders",
    "the frontend alias @ is written twice, in vite.config.ts and as @/* in tsconfig.json paths; shadcn components.json repeats @/components, @/lib and @/hooks",
    "frontend/tsconfig.json includes src, tests and playwright.config.ts and references tsconfig.node.json; tsconfig.build.json extends it, drops tests and is the one the build script passes to tsc",
    "frontend/src/components/ui/ is shadcn code copied into the project and skipped by biome.json: it is project code, not vendored",
    "the route /api/v1/private/users/ exists only when FASTAPI_ENV is development (backend/app/api/main.py), yet the generated client and the Playwright tests use it",
    ".agents/skills/fastapi and .claude/skills/sqlmodel are symlinks into ../../.venv/lib/python3.14/site-packages: they dangle in a fresh clone",
    "backend/app/alembic/script.py.mako is Mako, not Python; alembic/versions/ are migrations kept in the repository and count as project code",
    "hooks/post_gen_project.py is a template generator hook that rewrites line endings of *.sh files; no build step runs it",
    "Sentry, SMTP and FastAPI Cloud are named only by a client package, settings and a workflow: none has a compose service",
    "languages lists programming and markup languages only; JSON, YAML, TOML and Markdown files are present and not listed",
    "connections is a sample of 29 points: every route of the generated client, the OpenAPI document the client is generated from, the two build outputs written into backend/app, the database, the Mailpit API used by tests and the shared Biome configuration"
  ]
}
